10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Guillermo del Toro's Pinocchio (or simply Pinocchio) is a 2022 animated musical dark fantasy film directed by Guillermo del Toro
and Mark Gustafson, from a story by Matthew Robbins and del Toro, and a screenplay by del Toro and Patrick McHale.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
It is loosely based on Carlo Collodi's 1883 Italian novel The Adventures of Pinocchio, with the
title character's design strongly influenced by illustrator Gris Grimly's work.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Set in Fascist Italy during the interwar period, the story follows Pinocchio, a
wooden puppet who comes to life as the son of his carver, Geppetto.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The film stars the voice of Gregory Mann as Pinocchio and David Bradley as Geppetto, alongside Ewan McGregor, Burn Gorman, Ron
Perlman, John Turturro, Finn Wolfhard, Cate Blanchett, Tim Blake Nelson, Christoph Waltz, and Tilda Swinton.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Pinocchio was the final film credited to Gustafson before his death in 2024.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
A longtime passion project for del Toro, who considers that no other character ever "had as deep of a
personal connection to [him]" as Pinocchio, the film is dedicated to the memories of his parents.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It was originally announced in 2008 with a release in 2013 or 2014.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
However, it went into development hell.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
In January 2017, McHale was announced to co-write the screenplay, but production was
suspended in November 2017 as no studios were willing to provide financing.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
It was revived the following year after being acquired by Netflix.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Pinocchio premiered at the 66th BFI London Film Festival on October 15, 2022.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
It was released in select theaters on November 9, and
began streaming on Netflix on December 9.

22
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
The film received widespread critical acclaim for its direction, writing, voice performances, animation,
production design, musical numbers, and faithfulness in retaining the darkness of the source material.

23
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:36,000
Among its numerous accolades, Pinocchio won Best Animated Feature category at the Academy
Awards, BAFTA Awards, Golden Globe Awards, Critic's Choice Awards and PGA Awards.

24
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
italy, fascism, greed, woodcutter.

25
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
The tone is dark and emotional.
